# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# XO Club Dubai / ahmedxoclub.com — environment template
# Copy to `.env` on the server (never commit the real `.env`).
#
#   cp .env.example .env && nano .env
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Prisma / SQLite.
#
# DEVELOPMENT (relative is fine — src/lib/db.ts pins it to the project root):
#   DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"          →  <projectRoot>/db/custom.db
#
# PRODUCTION: use an ABSOLUTE path inside the app directory:
#   DATABASE_URL="file:/home/uXXXXXXXXX/domains/ahmedxoclub.com/app/db/custom.db"
#
# Why it matters: Prisma resolves a RELATIVE `file:` URL against the *schema*
# directory, while the running server resolves it against its *cwd*, so a
# relative URL makes the CLI and the app open two different files. A stale
# absolute path produces `Error code 14: Unable to open the database file`.
# `npm run db:push` resolves relative paths the same way the app does.
DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"

# Runtime (only needed if your process manager does not set them).
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
HOSTNAME=127.0.0.1

# Optional: bump if Next needs more heap during `next build`.
# NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2048
